DESCRIPTION:Event by Community Arts of Elmira\nCommunity Arts of Elmira\nD
 uration: 1 hr 30 min\nPublic\nSave-the-Date for "Wreathe Bingo" An Older A
 dult/Caregiver Free Arts Wellness Event!\nThe Third "Learn\, Explore\, Cre
 ate\, Connect (LECC): An Interactive Wellness Event for Older Adults and C
 aregivers" takes place Wednesday/November 18\, 2026\, 1:30-3:00pm. Registe
 r at 607-737-5520/Chemung County Department of Aging and Long Term Care.\n
 People not only will play "Wreath Bingo" for the chance to take home a har
 dy plant\, but also have the opportunity to paint holiday ornaments with A
 rtist Jennifer Sekella to enhance what plants they might already have at h
 ome! LECC is a wellness open house offering access to essential\, best-car
 e resources in a supportive environment for all participants\, who can eng
 age with professionals from the host organizations onsite to learn and ask
  questions\, while making new connections with people facing similar life 
 challenges and searching for help.\nThank you to Artist Filomena Jack of F
 ilomena Jack Studion for creating this flier.\nHosted by the Alzheimer's A
 ssociation\, Chemung County Department of Aging and Long Term Care and Com
 munity Arts of Elmira!\nLocation: Community Arts of Elmira\, 413 Lake Stre
 et\, Elmira\, New York 14901\, on the Elmira Creative Corridor\n#creativec
 ommunitypartnership\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0
 uzpj/event/78508394/20261118133000
GEO:42.09354;-76.804137
LOCATION:Community Arts of Elmira\, 413 Lake Street\, Elmira\, New York\, 
 14901\, United States
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78508394/20261118133000
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BraVESTimo! Dementia and Community Chorus
DTSTART:20261118T183000Z
DTEND:20261118T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20261118T175952Z
UID:df70f963ad217089b3237d1ba21b6b895ca19aaf@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music,Causes,Community
DESCRIPTION:Event by VEST - Vocal Essence of the Southern Tier and The Par
 k Church Elmira\nThe Park Church Elmira\nPublic\nSinging is good for the b
 rain—and even better when we experience it together!\nBraVESTimo! is a j
 oyful community chorus for people living with dementia\, Parkinson’s dis
 ease\, or other neurodegenerative conditions\, their care partners\, and c
 ommunity members who simply love to sing.\nYou do not need to have a perso
 nal connection to dementia to participate. Community singers are warmly in
 vited to sing alongside our members—adding friendship\, encouragement\, 
 musical support\, and shared joy.\nResearch suggests that group singing ca
 n support mood\, meaningful engagement\, emotional well-being\, and social
  connection for people living with dementia and their care partners.\nThis
  is not a choir performing for people living with dementia. It is a commun
 ity singing with one another.\nNo prior singing experience is needed. All 
 voices are welcome.\nLearn more and register at www.vestny.org.\nWe offer 
 barrier-free access with a Pay-What-You-Are-Able Model\n#BraVESTimo #Commu
 nitySinging #DementiaSupport #CarePartners #BrainHealth #MusicAndMemory #V
 ESTNY\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/785
 14637/20261118133000
GEO:42.089201;-76.808797
LOCATION:Park Church\, 208 West Gray Street\, Elmira\, New York\, 14901\, 
 United States
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78514637/20261118133000
END:VEVENT
